  "id": "secondskin",
  "neon": "#ff2e8e",
  "note": "A boutique on the west strip. Two storeys CANTILEVERED off each other over a glazed shopfront, under a small centred chamfer — the cheapest way to break a low silhouette without pretending a two-floor shop is a tower. ⚠ A CANTILEVER AND A ROTATION NEVER SHARE A SEGMENT — see the warning in aurelia.json. An offset box and a yawed box are each safe; a box that is both puts the derived kit where its own solid is not, and glself catches it. So asymmetry here is offset-only and every chamfer is CENTRED. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the boutique arm back.",
